WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.800
As our heroes continue to make their way to Anistar City,

2
00:00:05.866 --> 00:00:09.466
they soon arrive at the foot of Mount Molteau.

3
00:00:11.366 --> 00:00:13.066
A volcano?

4
00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:15.466
- Think that mountain could be one?
- Pika!

5
00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:20.033
I do. Up there, see the smoke coming out near the top?

6
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.766
Yeah. Wow!

7
00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:23.466
-Pika?

8
00:00:23.533 --> 00:00:24.666
Charm...

9
00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:28.966
- Hey, do you hear that noise?
- Serena, could it be a Pokémon?

10
00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.566
Charm.

11
00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:34.100
- What Pokémon is that?
- It's a Charmeleon.

12
00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:35.500
Charmeleon?

13
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.233
Charmeleon. The Flame Pokémon, and the evolved form of Charmander.

14
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.666
Charmeleon knocks down opponents with its tail,

15
00:00:43.733 --> 00:00:45.533
then defeats them using razor-sharp claws.

16
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.066
- Charm.
- Pika, pika!

17
00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.900
- Hey, Pikachu!
- Dedenne!

18
00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:52.066
Charmeleon!

19
00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:54.500
Pi, pi, Pika!

20
00:00:54.566 --> 00:00:56.533
-Pikachu, are you OK?

21
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:57.733
Pikachu.

22
00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.533
- Hey, why did you have to do that?
- Charmeleon!

23
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.300
Huh? Oh, there you are, Charmeleon.

24
00:01:03.366 --> 00:01:05.200
Meleon!

25
00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:12.033
I know that voice. Trevor? Is that you?

26
00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.866
Yeah.

27
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.800
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

28
00:01:15.866 --> 00:01:17.566
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

29
00:01:17.633 --> 00:01:21.000
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

30
00:01:21.066 --> 00:01:22.466
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

31
00:01:22.533 --> 00:01:26.300
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

32
00:01:26.366 --> 00:01:29.566
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

33
00:01:29.633 --> 00:01:33.000
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

34
00:01:33.066 --> 00:01:36.966
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

35
00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:41.666
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

36
00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:43.933
♪ Pokémon! ♪

37
00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.233
A Legendary Photo Op!

38
00:01:53.566 --> 00:01:57.866
Whoa, what a surprise. I never thought I'd run into you out here.

39
00:01:57.933 --> 00:02:00.533
Charm!

40
00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.433
Why does Charmeleon seem to be in such an awful mood?

41
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.733
And it's like that, no matter what I do.

42
00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.966
Maybe Charmeleon wants to have a Pokémon battle.

43
00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:11.233
Yeah? Is that what you want, Charmeleon?

44
00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.466
Charmeleon!

45
00:02:12.533 --> 00:02:15.366
Great! Just leave it to me, OK?

46
00:02:15.433 --> 00:02:17.933
Fletchinder, come on out.

47
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.166
Fletch!

48
00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:23.166
A good battle ought to be just the thing to calm Charmeleon right down.

49
00:02:23.233 --> 00:02:26.866
Thank you so much, Ash. A battle should do the trick.

50
00:02:26.933 --> 00:02:28.166
Meleon.

51
00:02:31.733 --> 00:02:33.033
OK. Let's do it.

52
00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:35.300
OK, Charmeleon, ready to go?

53
00:02:35.366 --> 00:02:36.966
Charmeleon!

54
00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.933
All right, let's start out with Fire Spin.

55
00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.266
Meleon!

56
00:02:45.333 --> 00:02:46.966
Quick, get out of there, now!

57
00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.233
Fletchinder!

58
00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:51.600
- Now use Flamethrower.
- Charm!

59
00:02:51.666 --> 00:02:54.366
Deflect it with Steel Wing.

60
00:02:54.433 --> 00:02:56.033
Fletchinder!

61
00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.133
You've got an opening. Use Flame Charge.

62
00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:02.166
Fletchinder!

63
00:03:05.233 --> 00:03:06.400
Chinder!

64
00:03:06.466 --> 00:03:08.500
- So cool.
- Denne!

65
00:03:08.566 --> 00:03:12.633
- Charmeleon's really something.
- It's definitely been well trained.

66
00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:15.433
Charmeleon, use Dragon Claw.

67
00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.166
Charm, charm, charm, charm, charm, charm!

68
00:03:18.233 --> 00:03:20.166
- Fletch!
- Charmeleon!

69
00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.100
Chinder!

70
00:03:22.166 --> 00:03:23.233
Tough stuff.

71
00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.533
- Now's your chance. Use Flamethrower.
- Charm!

72
00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.133
- Up in the air.
- Fletch! Fletchinder!

73
00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.333
- Aah!
- Now, use Steel Wing, let's go.

74
00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:35.766
Fletch! Fletchinder!

75
00:03:35.833 --> 00:03:37.400
Fletch!

76
00:03:37.466 --> 00:03:39.733
Chinder!

77
00:03:41.466 --> 00:03:43.133
Meleon.

78
00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.633
And that is it.

79
00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:48.433
- Oh, no. Charmeleon, are you all right?
- Charm.

80
00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:51.866
- Fletchinder, you were awesome.
- Fletchinder!

81
00:03:51.933 --> 00:03:53.433
Feeling better now?

82
00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.433
-Charm!

83
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.366
- Yay, you're feeling better.
- Denne!

84
00:03:59.433 --> 00:04:03.800
- Charmeleon, that's wonderful.
- You're all the best. Thanks.

85
00:04:03.866 --> 00:04:05.800
-Meleon!

86
00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:10.366
- Fletchinder! Fletchinder!
- Pika, pika!

87
00:04:10.433 --> 00:04:13.966
Last I saw you guys was at Pokémon summer camp, am I right?

88
00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:17.733
Uh-huh. That was so much fun. We had a really great time.

89
00:04:22.966 --> 00:04:27.500
Charmeleon evolved from Charmander, but its personality hasn't changed a bit.

90
00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:30.366
Charmeleon's been unbelievable in Gym Battles,

91
00:04:30.433 --> 00:04:33.766
and thanks to all of its hard work, I even earned a Bug Badge.

92
00:04:33.833 --> 00:04:36.833
Wow, that means you beat Viola.

93
00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.133
Obviously, you're working hard.

94
00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:43.033
Yeah, but not just me. Shauna and Tierno are working real hard too.

95
00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.200
- Aah! Tierno's right.
- Huh?

96
00:04:45.266 --> 00:04:47.200
- You do look great.
- I do?

97
00:04:47.266 --> 00:04:49.233
It's just that I got a message from Tierno

98
00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.833
telling me that your clothes and hair are looking amazing these days.

99
00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.866
How nice. Thanks.

100
00:04:55.933 --> 00:04:59.000
So have you all come here looking for Moltres too?

101
00:04:59.066 --> 00:05:00.766
- Moltres?
- Pika, pika, pika.

102
00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:02.233
Am I wrong?

103
00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.433
- You mean the Legendary Pokémon?
- Legendary?

104
00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.733
Articuno, Zapdos and Moltres.

105
00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:12.066
They're Pokémon whose existence has already been confirmed,

106
00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:15.166
but who appear to be extraordinarily difficult to track down.

107
00:05:15.233 --> 00:05:18.666
- I wanna meet Moltres too.
- Denne-ne!

108
00:05:18.733 --> 00:05:22.166
An examination and analysis of various documents

109
00:05:22.233 --> 00:05:25.100
leads me to believe that Moltres is on Mount Molteau.

110
00:05:25.166 --> 00:05:27.766
You wanna take a picture of it, don't you?

111
00:05:27.833 --> 00:05:31.733
Right. It's always been my dream to meet every Pokémon in the Pokédex

112
00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.033
and add them all to my photo collection.

113
00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.533
See this?

114
00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.766
Zapdos. And Articuno.

115
00:05:37.833 --> 00:05:40.800
- Pika!
- No way. You've met Legendary Pokémon?

116
00:05:40.866 --> 00:05:42.833
- Not fair.
- Denne!

117
00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.166
- Incredible, Trevor.
- Pika, pika!

118
00:05:45.233 --> 00:05:46.466
If I can get Moltres,

119
00:05:46.533 --> 00:05:50.333
I'll have taken photos of each of these three Legendary Pokémon.

120
00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.466
And check this out.

121
00:05:52.533 --> 00:05:56.466
Look. Aren't these Scatterbug really rare?

122
00:05:56.533 --> 00:06:00.666
- Why are they rare?
- They look like normal Scatterbug.

123
00:06:00.733 --> 00:06:04.233
What are you talking about? Just look at the antennae.

124
00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.900
See? The lengths are ever so slightly different.

125
00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:10.166
- Wow, are they?
- Subtle, but they're not the same.

126
00:06:10.233 --> 00:06:13.400
- Hold on. That's important?
- Sure is.

127
00:06:13.466 --> 00:06:16.533
You see, it's almost impossible to find this kind of Scatterbug.

128
00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:20.033
You can't get any more rare than these two.

129
00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.633
Yup, this is a picture almost no one gets.

130
00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:25.266
I've also got a Whiscash with straight whiskers

131
00:06:25.333 --> 00:06:27.133
who's only been spotted at Eur Lake.

132
00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:28.433
Then there's this Golem.

133
00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.633
The pattern of its shell and body are slightly unusual.

134
00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.900
It's only been confirmed recently. So few know of it,

135
00:06:33.966 --> 00:06:35.833
I had a really hard time getting this picture.

136
00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.733
This rare Sableye with a crystal eye

137
00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:39.733
that's slightly darker than usual is rare too.

138
00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:43.666
Anyway, that's what I have so far. So you all get it now, huh?

139
00:06:44.766 --> 00:06:47.900
-You bet. You've met all kinds of Pokémon.

140
00:06:47.966 --> 00:06:51.966
Right. And Moltres is going to be the very next photograph I take.

141
00:06:52.033 --> 00:06:54.400
We'll help you look for Moltres, if you want.

142
00:06:54.466 --> 00:06:55.500
Pikachu!

143
00:06:55.566 --> 00:06:58.466
- It'll be much faster that way.
- I wanna see too.

144
00:06:58.533 --> 00:07:01.266
- Yay. And don't forget me.
- Thank you.

145
00:07:01.333 --> 00:07:02.800
That would be a big help.

146
00:07:03.766 --> 00:07:06.800
That picto-twerp is quite a go-getter, isn't he?

147
00:07:06.866 --> 00:07:10.933
Yeah. I never would've imagined Moltres is hanging out on this mountain.

148
00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.400
If we were to procure a Legendary Pokémon,

149
00:07:13.466 --> 00:07:17.033
Team Rocket could ride a one-way ticket to Successville.

150
00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.066
Grabbin' Pikachu would be a breeze,

151
00:07:19.133 --> 00:07:21.700
and our grateful boss would be ever so pleased.

152
00:07:21.766 --> 00:07:25.633
But catching Moltres is job number one. So let's get that job done.

153
00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:27.000
What fun.

154
00:07:27.066 --> 00:07:28.433
Wobbuffet!

155
00:07:30.666 --> 00:07:32.600
- This is Moltres, for sure?

156
00:07:32.666 --> 00:07:34.466
Yup. No doubt about it.

157
00:07:34.533 --> 00:07:38.833
But it's really hard to see anything. How do you know? Huh?

158
00:07:39.766 --> 00:07:42.900
There's no other Pokémon with wings shaped just like that.

159
00:07:42.966 --> 00:07:44.833
And according to my research,

160
00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.833
Moltres has been spotted on Mount Molteau in the past.

161
00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:51.700
It was an accident that Moltres got in there in the first place.

162
00:07:51.766 --> 00:07:54.033
It didn't even know it was being photographed.

163
00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:57.766
But if we head up to that big rock, I know we'll see it.

164
00:07:57.833 --> 00:07:59.366
Hm.

165
00:07:59.433 --> 00:08:01.933
So that's all we have to go on, huh?

166
00:08:04.533 --> 00:08:08.266
So we're headed to a big rock. I'd say this is my cue.

167
00:08:08.333 --> 00:08:11.433
And that means the future is now, thanks to science.

168
00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:13.666
Clemontic Gear, on.

169
00:08:13.733 --> 00:08:17.666
I thought that we'd encounter a situation precisely like this one.

170
00:08:17.733 --> 00:08:20.300
This is called my Rock Searcher Mark One.

171
00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:24.466
- Rock Searcher Mark One?
- You think it's gonna work this time?

172
00:08:24.533 --> 00:08:25.533
Denne-ne?

173
00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:29.066
Oh, wow. This is one of your famous inventions.

174
00:08:29.133 --> 00:08:31.066
-Pika!

175
00:08:32.866 --> 00:08:36.566
I input the landscape of this photograph into its memory.

176
00:08:36.633 --> 00:08:40.533
Then my amazing device will locate an exact match automatically.

177
00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:42.133
Awesome.

178
00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.800
Please save the praise for later, my good friend.

179
00:08:44.866 --> 00:08:48.533
After we discover Moltres's location, you can thank me.

180
00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:50.633
Rock Searcher Mark One, on.

181
00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:52.533
-Pika!

182
00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:55.800
- Science is so amazing.
- Pika, pika!

183
00:08:55.866 --> 00:08:57.966
Let's go say hi to Moltres.

184
00:08:58.033 --> 00:08:59.266
Denne!

185
00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.666
Let's stick to 'em like glue.

186
00:09:02.733 --> 00:09:03.900
Woo-hoo.

187
00:09:03.966 --> 00:09:05.500
Wobbuffet!

188
00:09:13.133 --> 00:09:14.666
-That's it?

189
00:09:14.733 --> 00:09:16.133
- Pika?
- Huh?

190
00:09:21.333 --> 00:09:24.866
- Looks like it's not a match.
- But it's still looking around.

191
00:09:33.266 --> 00:09:36.000
Tres!

192
00:09:36.066 --> 00:09:38.733
Who's that Pokémon?

193
00:09:43.266 --> 00:09:46.333
It's Charmeleon!

194
00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:48.400
Charm!

195
00:10:01.933 --> 00:10:04.266
Doesn't look like it's having too much luck.

196
00:10:04.333 --> 00:10:06.600
- Pika.
- Hm? Aah!

197
00:10:06.666 --> 00:10:10.300
- What's that?
- Oh, that's just a Crustle.

198
00:10:10.366 --> 00:10:14.100
Look closer. You don't see that kind of complex patterned layering

199
00:10:14.166 --> 00:10:16.266
- hardly ever.
- Huh?

200
00:10:16.333 --> 00:10:19.933
- So cool.
- Huh? Look!

201
00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.666
The tips of that Butterfree's antennae are slightly smaller than normal.

202
00:10:23.733 --> 00:10:26.400
That's rare. No, that's super-rare.

203
00:10:26.466 --> 00:10:30.033
I never dreamed I would run into a Butterfree like that here.

204
00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.400
How lucky can I get?

205
00:10:32.466 --> 00:10:34.366
- Pika.
- I would say this particular area

206
00:10:34.433 --> 00:10:36.666
is a Pokémon photographer's paradise.

207
00:10:38.166 --> 00:10:41.200
-Wrong again.

208
00:10:41.266 --> 00:10:44.900
- Trevor. Let's go.
- Please, just one more minute.

209
00:10:44.966 --> 00:10:49.100
- This is incredible.
- I think he's forgotten about Moltres.

210
00:10:49.166 --> 00:10:52.366
He works so hard. Photography seems tough.

211
00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:56.566
Now's our chance to get to Moltres before the twerps do.

212
00:10:56.633 --> 00:10:57.800
Ooh!

213
00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:04.633
Huh?

214
00:11:05.633 --> 00:11:07.466
It stopped in its tracks.

215
00:11:07.533 --> 00:11:11.566
- What's wrong? Getting lazy?
- Maybe it's on the fritz.

216
00:11:11.633 --> 00:11:15.333
If that's true, we won't be able to procure Moltres or Pikachu.

217
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.333
Who's at the door?

218
00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:24.433
- It's a warning bell.
- You stupid... Gah!

219
00:11:28.533 --> 00:11:30.300
- Pika!
- What was that?

220
00:11:30.366 --> 00:11:32.566
Not my Rock Searcher Mark One!

221
00:11:32.633 --> 00:11:34.666
Let's go find out.

222
00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.033
Rock Searcher Mark Done.

223
00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:41.233
Twerps closin' in fast.

224
00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.333
Unh... Aah!

225
00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:45.866
I knew it.

226
00:11:45.933 --> 00:11:48.300
Another one bites the dust.

227
00:11:48.366 --> 00:11:50.900
Now we'll never find out where Moltres is.

228
00:11:50.966 --> 00:11:53.366
- Pika!
- Oh, no.

229
00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:07.233
- Clemont, what's going on?
- It's gone completely haywire.

230
00:12:15.966 --> 00:12:18.700
- Are you OK, Pikachu?
- Pikachu.

231
00:12:18.766 --> 00:12:20.600
-Pikachu, no.

232
00:12:20.666 --> 00:12:22.966
- Pika, pika!
- Heh, Pikachu, yes.

233
00:12:23.033 --> 00:12:24.366
Team Rocket.

234
00:12:24.433 --> 00:12:27.100
Prepare for trouble, that certainly went well!

235
00:12:27.166 --> 00:12:29.466
And make it double, success is swell!

236
00:12:29.533 --> 00:12:32.000
To protect our work and all it achieves!

237
00:12:32.066 --> 00:12:34.500
To expose our roles as Pikachu thieves!

238
00:12:34.566 --> 00:12:37.800
To denounce the evils of taking appalling pics!

239
00:12:37.866 --> 00:12:41.100
To watch you lie there like a ton of bricks!

240
00:12:41.166 --> 00:12:43.233
- Jessie!
- And James.

241
00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:46.533
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light!

242
00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:49.400
Surrender now or prepare for a photo-finish fight!

243
00:12:49.466 --> 00:12:52.566
- Meowth, that's right!
- Wobbuffet!

244
00:12:54.466 --> 00:12:57.133
- So you followed us again.
- Perceptive.

245
00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:00.166
The plan was to make Moltres into one of our associates.

246
00:13:00.233 --> 00:13:02.966
But, since the odds of you finding it are zero,

247
00:13:03.033 --> 00:13:05.400
we'll take Pikachu and call it a day.

248
00:13:05.466 --> 00:13:06.966
Fletchinder, let's go.

249
00:13:10.033 --> 00:13:13.233
- Fletchinder!
- Two can play at that game.

250
00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:15.166
The game is rigged in our favour.

251
00:13:16.033 --> 00:13:17.700
- Gourgeist, Shadow Ball.
- Gourgeist!

252
00:13:17.766 --> 00:13:19.000
- OK, Inkay, Psybeam!
- Ink!

253
00:13:19.066 --> 00:13:21.800
- Gourgeist!
- Inkay!

254
00:13:21.866 --> 00:13:26.433
- Fletchinder. Dodge it, quick.
- Fletch! Fletchinder! Fletch! Fletch!

255
00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:30.233
That Gourgeist's size is totally rare.

256
00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:32.933
Trevor? Save the pics for another time.

257
00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:36.866
You're right. Charmeleon, now. Use Flamethrower.

258
00:13:36.933 --> 00:13:38.833
- Charm!
- Deflect it with Psybeam.

259
00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:40.900
Inkay!

260
00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:46.100
- Wrap it up, Gourgeist. Done.
- We've had enough fun.

261
00:13:46.166 --> 00:13:47.233
- Psybeam, go.
- Shadow Ball.

262
00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:48.866
Gourgeist!

263
00:13:48.933 --> 00:13:50.500
- Dodge it.
- Fletchin! Chinder!

264
00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:55.533
- Shadow Ball. Once more with feeling.
- And it's Psybeam for the win.

265
00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:58.700
Fletchinder! Fletch!

266
00:13:58.766 --> 00:14:00.933
Chinder! Fletch!

267
00:14:05.733 --> 00:14:07.666
Will you stop being a moving target?

268
00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:10.666
Moltres!

269
00:14:10.733 --> 00:14:13.166
Fletch! Fletchinder!

270
00:14:13.233 --> 00:14:15.133
Huh? What's that?

271
00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:18.866
Moltres!

272
00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:24.000
- It sounded like a roar to me.
- I'm scared.

273
00:14:24.066 --> 00:14:26.300
You don't think that's...

274
00:14:29.366 --> 00:14:32.733
Gourgeist!

275
00:14:37.966 --> 00:14:42.800
Whoa! Could that be the Legendary Pokémon?

276
00:14:42.866 --> 00:14:44.566
Is it Moltres?

277
00:14:45.733 --> 00:14:47.566
Mol!

278
00:14:47.633 --> 00:14:52.133
So Moltres was here, hiding in the volcano's magma all along.

279
00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.033
Incredible.

280
00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:56.300
I've heard about that before.

281
00:14:56.366 --> 00:14:59.000
It's said that Moltres rests in volcano lava

282
00:14:59.066 --> 00:15:02.333
in order to build up its power.

283
00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:05.700
We finally meet. It's like a dream.

284
00:15:12.666 --> 00:15:16.433
OK, we're going back to Plan A. Let's take Moltres away.

285
00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:19.133
- OK, Inkay.
- Gourgeist.

286
00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.566
- Shadow Ball.
- Psybeam.

287
00:15:20.633 --> 00:15:22.233
- Inkay!
- Gourgeist!

288
00:15:24.566 --> 00:15:26.933
Moltres.

289
00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:31.533
There's no doubt about it. That's one legendary Flamethrower.

290
00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:33.333
Why don't you write a fan letter?

291
00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:36.866
Who'd have thought grabbing Pikachu would've been our second choice?

292
00:15:36.933 --> 00:15:40.666
- We're blasting off again!
- Wobbuffet!

293
00:15:40.733 --> 00:15:42.733
Inkay!

294
00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:44.866
Pikachu!

295
00:15:44.933 --> 00:15:49.100
Quick, Fletchinder. Use Steel Wing. Break Pikachu out of there.

296
00:15:49.233 --> 00:15:51.633
Fletchinder!

297
00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:53.433
Pika, pi!

298
00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:56.566
- Pikachu! Hey, buddy.
- Pi! Pikachu!

299
00:15:56.633 --> 00:15:59.433
- Fletchinder, thanks a lot.
- Chinder. Fletch.

300
00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:00.800
Moltres.

301
00:16:03.966 --> 00:16:07.900
Unh! I'll bet Moltres thinks we're friends with Team Rocket.

302
00:16:07.966 --> 00:16:10.733
- No way.
- Stop it. We're not your enemies.

303
00:16:10.866 --> 00:16:13.366
- Tres!
- Pika!

304
00:16:13.433 --> 00:16:15.666
Unh! Gotta do it. Frogadier, go.

305
00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:18.766
Frogadier!

306
00:16:18.833 --> 00:16:22.300
- All right, Frogadier, Water Pulse.
- Froga!

307
00:16:24.866 --> 00:16:26.033
- What happened?
- Pika?

308
00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:29.200
- It evaporated?
- So let's try fire.

309
00:16:29.266 --> 00:16:32.433
- Charmeleon, Flamethrower, now!
- Charm!

310
00:16:34.633 --> 00:16:37.300
Moltres!

311
00:16:37.966 --> 00:16:40.133
- Dodge it, quick!
- Fletchinder!

312
00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:43.900
Fletch! Fletch!

313
00:16:43.966 --> 00:16:45.466
Chinder!

314
00:16:45.533 --> 00:16:48.200
Moltres!

315
00:16:49.666 --> 00:16:53.266
- No! Fletchinder, are you OK?
- Chinder...

316
00:16:53.333 --> 00:16:54.833
Fletchinder...

317
00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:55.900
-Dier.

318
00:16:55.966 --> 00:16:57.233
- Ash!
- Pika, pi!

319
00:16:57.300 --> 00:17:00.300
Trevor, let me go! Fletchinder, I'm coming!

320
00:17:01.733 --> 00:17:03.333
-Res!

321
00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:05.466
- Aaah!
- Oh, no.

322
00:17:05.533 --> 00:17:07.633
Fletchinder!

323
00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:10.599
- Fletch! Fletch! Fletch!
- Aaah!

324
00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:14.933
Fletchin!

325
00:17:21.099 --> 00:17:22.833
Pika?

326
00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:26.800
-Pika.

327
00:17:26.866 --> 00:17:28.333
- Gadier.
- Could it be...

328
00:17:35.133 --> 00:17:39.000
Aah! It's evolving. Awesome.

329
00:17:39.133 --> 00:17:42.500
- Flame!
- Mol.

330
00:17:42.566 --> 00:17:44.633
Ah!

331
00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:47.166
Talonflame. The Scorching Pokémon,

332
00:17:47.233 --> 00:17:48.933
and the evolved form of Fletchinder.

333
00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.333
During an intense battle,

334
00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:53.133
Talonflame expels embers from gaps between its feathers.

335
00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:56.866
It reaches speeds of more than 300 miles per hour chasing prey.

336
00:17:56.933 --> 00:17:58.800
Wow! A Talonflame.

337
00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:01.633
Talon.

338
00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:03.566
Here it comes.

339
00:18:03.633 --> 00:18:06.766
Talonflame!

340
00:18:06.833 --> 00:18:09.466
- What was that?
- That was Brave Bird.

341
00:18:09.533 --> 00:18:13.733
Brave Bird is, without a doubt, one of the most powerful of all Flying-type moves.

342
00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:16.066
Whoa, really?

343
00:18:16.133 --> 00:18:17.733
Res!

344
00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:20.333
Now, Talonflame, use Brave Bird.

345
00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:24.900
Talonflame!

346
00:18:24.966 --> 00:18:28.200
- Moltres!
- Talonflame!

347
00:18:28.266 --> 00:18:32.300
- Talonflame!
- Mol!

348
00:18:32.366 --> 00:18:35.733
It's so fast.

349
00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:39.466
- Talonflame!
- Res!

350
00:18:42.633 --> 00:18:44.566
Talonflame!

351
00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:48.400
- Ash, hold on!

352
00:18:55.066 --> 00:18:57.266
Frogadier!

353
00:19:01.666 --> 00:19:05.433
- Ash, oh no!
- Frogadier, pull them up fast.

354
00:19:08.066 --> 00:19:10.166
Talonflame, are you all right?

355
00:19:10.233 --> 00:19:12.666
Flame. Talonflame.

356
00:19:16.466 --> 00:19:21.766
- Ash, that was a close one.
- You sure can be reckless sometimes.

357
00:19:21.833 --> 00:19:23.133
Yeah.

358
00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:24.566
- Heh.
- Pikachu!

359
00:19:24.633 --> 00:19:28.166
Sorry I scared you, Pikachu. Thanks a lot, Talonflame.

360
00:19:28.233 --> 00:19:30.266
Talonflame.

361
00:19:30.333 --> 00:19:32.300
-Pika?

362
00:19:38.066 --> 00:19:40.633
- Wow.
- It's leaving.

363
00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:44.666
Yeah. I think Moltres finally knows we're not actually enemies.

364
00:19:44.733 --> 00:19:47.300
- I wonder where it's going to go now.
- Pika.

365
00:20:06.333 --> 00:20:08.533
Cool. I got a great shot.

366
00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:11.933
Trevor, that's wonderful. I guess it was all worth it.

367
00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:15.033
- Denne.
- Yeah. I'm really glad.

368
00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:17.766
We've got a lot of things to do, Talonflame.

369
00:20:17.833 --> 00:20:19.600
- Let's work hard.
- Talon.

370
00:20:19.666 --> 00:20:21.766
- Pika, pika!
- Frog.

371
00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:26.133
Perfect. I'll add this to my collection.

372
00:20:27.800 --> 00:20:30.800
A trip to Mount Molteau has given our heroes the chance

373
00:20:30.866 --> 00:20:33.700
to meet the Legendary Pokémon Moltres.

374
00:20:33.766 --> 00:20:37.700
On top of that, Fletchinder has evolved into Talonflame.

375
00:20:37.766 --> 00:20:41.366
And so, with all kinds of new Pokémon yet to meet,

376
00:20:41.433 --> 00:20:47.366
and all kinds of new adventures yet to experience, the journey continues.
